{"name":"Azalea","hex":"#d73b5d","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Azalea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["the azaleas, numerous varieties of flowering shrubs of temperate climates\n A taxonomic genus within the family Ericaceae.\n A taxonomic subgenus within the family Ericaceae – Rhododendron subg. Azalea, now Rhododendron subg. Azaleastrum.","A taxonomic genus within the family Ericaceae."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Azalea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Azalea","blocks":[{"text":"Azaleas are flowering shrubs in the genus Rhododendron, particularly the former subgenera Tsutsusi (evergreen) and Pentanthera (deciduous). Azaleas bloom in the spring, their flowers often lasting several weeks. Shade tolerant, they prefer living near or under trees. They are part of the family Ericaceae."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Azalea"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/George_Taber_azalea.jpg/500px-George_Taber_azalea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/George_Taber_azalea.jpg/1280px-George_Taber_azalea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/George_Taber_azalea.jpg/500px-George_Taber_azalea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"cv. 'George Taber'","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeorge_Taber_azalea.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Mini_pink_azaleas_in_Maryland.jpg/500px-Mini_pink_azaleas_in_Maryland.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Mini_pink_azaleas_in_Maryland.jpg/1280px-Mini_pink_azaleas_in_Maryland.jpg?utm_so